00:06:34.720 --> 00:06:37.890
do the the unit in the
Get Ready For Grade Level

00:06:37.890 --> 00:06:39.990
before they do the corresponding unit

00:06:39.990 --> 00:06:41.290
in the grade level course.

00:06:42.270 --> 00:06:43.385
- Yeah, I think there's a lot of

00:06:43.385 --> 00:06:46.480
a couple of different
models that would work well.

00:06:46.480 --> 00:06:48.160
Currently since we're
in the summer doing it,

00:06:48.160 --> 00:06:51.370
doing the full course in the
summer is a great way to build,

00:06:51.370 --> 00:06:52.950
know that if you have you know,

00:06:52.950 --> 00:06:54.491
some time to spend on math this summer,

00:06:54.491 --> 00:06:58.040
these are the best things
to use that time on.

00:06:58.040 --> 00:06:59.900
And you could, could
do the complete course

00:06:59.900 --> 00:07:01.353
over the summer ahead of time.

00:07:01.353 --> 00:07:03.780
For teachers during the school year.

00:07:03.780 --> 00:07:06.780
I think there's a lot of
value in doing it in line.

00:07:06.780 --> 00:07:09.260
And so the way we've built the course is

00:07:09.260 --> 00:07:10.306
each of the units will say,

00:07:10.306 --> 00:07:14.170
like in sixth grade, get ready for ratios

00:07:14.170 --> 00:07:15.950
because we know all sixth
graders are gonna spend

00:07:15.950 --> 00:07:17.815
